================================================================================================
CLASSICAL SURFACE RESIDUAL -- anatomy
================================================================================================
  rms 0.4597 K, mean -0.0709 K, range -1.350 to +0.875 K
  thermocouple noise ~0.0097 K -> 100.0 % of the residual VARIANCE is model-form error, not measurement
  residual autocorrelation falls to 1/e at lag 423 s -> strongly correlated, NOT white

  Correlation of the residual against candidate drivers:
    surface rise (T_s - T_inf)   r = +0.4092
    instantaneous heat I^2       r = +0.1031
    |current|                    r = +0.0630
    ambient T_inf                r = -0.3268
    time                         r = +0.5083   <-- strong
    dT_s/dt                      r = -0.0050
    measured core-surface        r = +0.3963

  Interpretation guide:
    correlation with SURFACE RISE  -> h is not constant (temperature- or
                                      flow-dependent convection)
    correlation with I^2           -> the source model is wrong in shape
    correlation with dT_s/dt       -> a missing thermal mass, e.g. the can
                                      or the thermocouple's own dynamics
    correlation with TIME          -> a slow drift (ageing, flow change)

  Test: let h vary linearly with surface rise, h = h0 (1 + g*(T_s - T_inf)).
  This stays a CLASSICAL fit -- physics enforced exactly -- and uses only
  surface and ambient data.
